                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "229343905",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198047967222",
                            "num_reviews": 4,
                            "playtime_forever": 180,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 180,
                            "last_played": 1782924537
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wanted to like this game, I really did and it was starting off relatively strongly. It was going well, nothing amazing but interesting enough that I was excited to play it. That is until the second or third chapter, can't remember, where the agency for my character and previous choices were taken from me. No spoilers but I played my character trying to hide his power. I was given a choice to not admit to my power. Then on the literal next page, my character was not found out, was not proven to be lying or hiding something, but just blurts out the very thing I just chose not to reveal. It was very jarring and took me completely out of the story. What is the point of having the option only for my character to do the exact opposite? If he had been found out, if the plot had revealed him, I could do deal with that, but that's not what happened.",
